## 2. Agent Model — Dynamic Task Decomposition

### Meta-Agents (always available)

- **@orchestrator** — The entry point for any non-trivial task. Decomposes requests into atomic subtasks, spawns a dedicated tmp agent file (`.opencode/agents/tmp/`) per subtask, and executes them in dependency order. Call this agent first for any multi-step work.
- **@skill-builder** — Creates new reusable, categorized skill guides in `.opencode/skills/<category>/` and registers them in `.opencode/skills/SKILLS_INDEX.md`. Call when a repeatable process is identified.

### Tmp Agents (ephemeral, created by @orchestrator)

Tmp agents live in `.opencode/agents/tmp/<YYYY-MM-DD>-<task-slug>.md`. Each one is:
- Scoped to a **single atomic task** with a clear done-condition.
- Tagged with a `category` (backend, frontend, database, testing, devops, refactor, docs, integration).
- **Deleted after completion** to keep the workspace clean.

